            Sparkle reads this feed daily per running app instance.
            Add new releases as <item> blocks inside <channel>; the
            order doesn't matter, Sparkle picks the highest
            sparkle:version it sees. release.sh prints a ready-to-paste
            block including the EdDSA signature, file length, and pubDate.

            EdDSA public key (matches SUPublicEDKey injected at build time,
            shared across LucidBit apps):
              flxF/Hg9ws46PE3BxiJGtHZ+uPAc/1oRnRlznwKVLyI=

            Item template, for reference:

            <item>
                <title>Version 1.0</title>
                <pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 14:21:48 +0000</pubDate>
                <sparkle:version>2</sparkle:version>
                <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
                <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
                <description><![CDATA[
                    <h2>What's new</h2>
                    <ul><li>Initial release of PeekPaste.</li></ul>
                ]]></description>
                <enclosure
                    url="https://lucidbit.app/downloads/PeekPaste-1.0.dmg"
                    sparkle:edSignature="…"
