            </item>
        -->
        <item>
            <title>Version 1.0</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 00:37:37 +0000</pubDate>
            <!--
                Build 3 REPLACED build 2 rather than being added beside it.

                Both builds ship as PeekPaste-1.0.dmg — the filename carries the
                marketing version, not the build — so uploading build 3
                overwrote the file build 2's item pointed at. Its edSignature and
                length then described bytes that no longer existed, and Sparkle
                would have rejected the download it was being told to trust.
                Leaving a superseded item in place is only safe when its
                enclosure is still there.

                Nobody was on build 2, so replacing costs nothing. If a future
                release needs to keep older items alive, the DMG filename has to
                include the build number.

                Description unchanged: build 3 is still 1.0 to anyone reading
                this, and the notes below still describe it accurately.
            -->
            <sparkle:version>3</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <h2>What's new in 1.0</h2>
                <p>Initial release. Your clipboard, within reach — a screen-edge clipboard for macOS that lives quietly out of the way until you push your pointer to the edge.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Edge panel:</strong> push your pointer to the edge of the screen to reveal recent clips over your work. Choose the edge, set a dwell delay, or use a keyboard shortcut.</li>
                    <li><strong>Rich card types:</strong> code is syntax-highlighted, links carry their title and preview, colours become swatches, files remain files, screenshots keep their preview.</li>
                    <li><strong>Search inside screenshots:</strong> on-device text recognition finds text captured inside images.</li>
                    <li><strong>Space to preview:</strong> press Space on any card to see the whole clip in detail before you paste.</li>
                    <li><strong>Library window:</strong> full search, filters, categories, pins, edit mode, and preview.</li>
                    <li><strong>Private by design:</strong> everything stays on your Mac. No analytics, no sync service, no phone-home. Per-app rules let you blur or ignore sensitive apps.</li>
                    <li><strong>One-time purchase:</strong> $9.99 with a 7-day free trial.</li>
                </ul>
            ]]></description>
            <enclosure
                url="https://lucidbit.app/downloads/PeekPaste-1.0.dmg"
                sparkle:edSignature="m7NK1ZQrqA8ZXvu8W2i0ifEmaniH5cxyhSTPVJues5EXATg6J6BU6jdrwoYLb9ci+HZx6mEby2UWHIwk7ZHzAw==" length="11082675"
                type="application/octet-stream" />
        </item>
